{"shortDescription":"The Japanese yen strengthened past 154 per dollar on Tuesday, reaching its strongest level since February and reversing the bearish forces that pushed the currency to a 40-year low in July.The rally was driven by the unwinding of carry trades, expectations of capital repatriation and growing US pol…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The Japanese yen strengthened past 154 per dollar on Tuesday, reaching its strongest level since February and reversing the bearish forces that pushed the currency to a 40-year low in July."]},{"type":"p","children":["The rally was driven by the unwinding of carry trades, expectations of capital repatriation and growing US political pressure for Japan to support the yen through tighter monetary policy."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets now expect the Bank of Japan to raise interest rates this month, with an economic adviser to Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi saying the central bank is likely to hike rates in September and deliver another increase by January next year."]},{"type":"p","children":["The remarks highlight growing recognition within the Takaichi administration, which has previously favored a dovish approach, that further BOJ tightening may be necessary to curb excessive yen weakness."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, data showed Japanese wages rose at their fastest pace since 1997, strengthening expectations for a more hawkish BOJ policy stance."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:581758:0","title":"Yen Surges to 7-Month High","published":1788826276,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/japan/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:USDJPY","currency-logoid":"country/JP","base-currency-logoid":"country/US","logo":{"style":"pair","logoid":"country/US","logoid2":"country/JP"}},{"sym